common/rc: resolve _fs_sysfs_dname via /sys/dev/block, not the node name

The fs registers its sysfs directory under the kernel's name for the
device (e.g. /sys/fs/xfs/dm-0). _short_dev only produces that name when
/dev/mapper entries are udev-managed symlinks to ../dm-N; on a system
where libdevmapper creates real nodes (DM_DISABLE_UDEV=1, common in
minimal/containerized test rigs), it returns the map name and every
_get/_set_fs_sysfs_attr caller silently misses, failing ~90 dm-backed
tests. Resolve the device's maj:min through /sys/dev/block instead,
which is correct with or without udev; fall back to _short_dev if the
sysfs link is unavailable.

--- a/common/rc
+++ b/common/rc
@@ -5436,7 +5436,21 @@
 	btrfs)
 		_btrfs_get_fsid $dev ;;
 	*)
-		_short_dev $dev ;;
+		# The sysfs dir uses the kernel's device name (e.g. dm-0),
+		# which matches the node's basename only when /dev entries
+		# are udev-managed symlinks. Resolve via /sys/dev/block so
+		# dm nodes created without udev work too.
+		local majmin=$(stat -L -c '%t:%T' "$dev")
+		local kname=""
+		if [ -n "$majmin" ]; then
+			kname=$(basename "$(readlink -f \
+				"/sys/dev/block/$((0x${majmin%:*})):$((0x${majmin#*:}))")")
+		fi
+		if [ -n "$kname" ] && [ -e "/sys/dev/block/$((0x${majmin%:*})):$((0x${majmin#*:}))" ]; then
+			echo "$kname"
+		else
+			_short_dev $dev
+		fi ;;
 	esac
 }
 
